Summary (Today):
Today’s activities mainly focused on self-learning in React, where I revised core React concepts and explored a few new topics for deeper understanding. I worked on example-based practice to understand component structure, state management, and data flow. The learning was self-paced and emphasized hands-on coding rather than theory alone. This helped in strengthening my frontend development skills through practical implementation.
Outcomes:
By the end of the day, I improved my clarity on fundamental React concepts through revision and coding examples. I gained better confidence in building and understanding React components independently. The self-learning approach helped me identify areas that need more practice and improvement. Overall, the day enhanced my ability to apply React concepts effectively in real applications.
